18:["$","p","5",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"Bad council questions are the ones with one right answer or no judgment involved: what's the capital of France, write me a tweet, summarize this article. And if you already know the answer and just want validation, it will probably tell you things you don't want to hear, which is the point."}]
19:["$","h2","6",{"className":"mt-12 t-h3 text-ink","children":"The five advisors"}]
1a:["$","p","7",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"Each one is a thinking style, not a job title. They're built to create tension with each other."}]
1b:["$","ul","8",{"className":"mt-5 space-y-3","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The Contrarian looks for what's wrong, what's missing, what will fail. The friend who saves you from a bad deal by asking the questions you're avoiding."}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The First Principles Thinker ignores the surface question and asks what you're actually trying to solve. Sometimes the best thing you get out of it is hearing you're asking the wrong question entirely."}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The Expansionist looks for the upside everyone else is missing. What could be bigger, what adjacent opportunity is hiding, what's undervalued."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The Pragmatist cares about what actually ships. Resources, timeline, the realistic next step."}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The User Advocate speaks for the person on the other end, the customer or reader who has to feel the decision."}]]}]]}]
1c:["$","h2","9",{"className":"mt-12 t-h3 text-ink","children":"How to run it"}]
1d:["$","p","10",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"Install the skill, then trigger it on any real decision with a phrase like \"council this,\" \"pressure-test this,\" or \"stress-test this.\" The five advisors analyze your question independently, peer-review each other anonymously, and a chairman writes the final verdict. You walk away with the recommendation and exactly where the advisors disagree and why."}]
1e:["$","div","11",{"className":"mt-6 rounded-xl border border-accent/30 bg-accent/10 px-5 py-4 leading-[1.7] text-ink","children":"Grab the skill file at the top, drop it into your Claude setup, then say \"run the council\" on your next big decision and watch it argue with itself on your behalf."}]
